lwinzeler@uiuc.edu (Loren Winzeler) writes:

>In unix, is there a way to connect a running process, which you own, 
>to a different tty?  

the only way you can reconnect a process to a tty is if the process is
aware that the tty is there and does the reconnection itself. There's
no way to reconnect to any of your "standard" processes unless you
run it with some type of wrapper just in case you lose your connection.
